// Chasm Bridge: Rapier joints as a structure. A rope bridge of 20 timber
// planks, each plank a rigid body hinged to the next and the end planks pinned
// to two sea stacks, sags across a 24 m chasm 17 m above a lava lake. Loads
// drop onto it from chutes in the roof: an iron-cornered wood crate (the deck
// dips and sways under it), then a glass crate, a glass frame around a lattice
// of glass blocks, that shatters by Voronoi fracture on the planks and rains
// glittering shards into the lava. Charges rumble in the roof and knock loose
// a pale concrete slab that lands mid-span. The deck bows, the centre hinge (the
// only breakable joint, 20 kN) snaps, and both halves swing down like pendulums,
// slap the stack faces and hang from their unbreakable pins. The crate, slab
// and glass float on the lava (wood 60, concrete 240 vs lava 250); the crate
// chars and burns, and a last crate tumbles in for the closing hold. Lit from
// below: the lava, two lavafalls, two small lava spouts and torches, with blue
// glowshrooms on the roof and stacks for a cool rim. 10 cells per metre, 60
// ticks per second.
[scene]
name = chasm bridge
description = A 20-plank rope bridge of hinged rigid bodies sags over a lava lake. A wood crate, then a glass crate that shatters, then a concrete slab blasted from the roof land on it; the centre hinge snaps, the halves swing down and hang from their pins, and the wreckage floats and burns on the lava.
size = 720 420
seed = 0xb21d
ticks = 2100

[build]
fill 0 0 720 420 stone
// one big cavern: ragged roof, open down to the lava lake
terrain 0 720 50 10 37 air 318
circle 60 46 28 air
circle 165 38 24 air
circle 560 42 26 air
circle 665 48 28 air
// hanging roof mass over the chasm, ragged bottom around y 84
